WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.550
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.140
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.760
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.690
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.310
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.400
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.660
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.050
Hey, I just bought something like this in Harajuku!

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.550
Wait, Harajuku?

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.040
When? You should’ve invited me!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.830
Maybe I should go too!

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.350
Who are you going with? Maybe…

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:28.350
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.910
and the listed sponsors.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.340
The Last Local Train will soon depart.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.280
Wait!

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.640
I’ll ride!

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.810
Wait!

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.050
What? Wait a second…

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:50.970
No way!

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.370
What should I do?

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.180
No really, it was a misunderstanding.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.800
I didn’t mean anything wrong.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.520
Using money for prostitutes…

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.530
I didn’t think that at all!

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.680
I don’t care. Just make some money! Or else…

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.720
Young lady, where are you going?

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.160
I’ll keep it cheap, just for now!

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.280
What’re you doing?

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.860
Did you fail again?

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.440
Shut up!

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.370
Ouch!

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.870
It’s so hot tonight, I’ll steam.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.750
If you’re gonna say that take off that coat!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.370
I’m hotter watching you.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.920
How many years has it been
since you came to this city?

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:06.980
Huh?

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.980
By that face…

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.390
about 4-5 years?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.900
No offense,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.490
but isn’t it time you returned to your hometown?

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.750
Stop joking around!

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.790
As for me,

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.000
I’ll become a big-shot and strut around this Shinjuku!

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.510
Until that becomes reality…

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:29.770
I’ll never go home!

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:34.820
Here.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.870
Oh! What is this?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.560
When you live like me

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.530
you sometimes want to be nice to someone else.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.590
What the hell are you talking about?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.010
When you’re nice to someone…

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.100
…you’re not at the bottom of existence.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.590
It means you still have things to spare.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.290
You can believe that.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:11.960
This uses a card too…

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.350
How cute!

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.480
Go! Go! Go!

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.840
What? What? What?

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:36.400
Yes!

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.850
Almost… Come on!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:45.600
Awww… It was almost there!

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.900
OK!

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.840
Hey you, aren’t you in middle school?

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.210
What’re you doing this late?

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.600
The last train already left.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.160
Say your address and phone number.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.660
Hey, wait a sec!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.550
I’ll go look for others.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:12.590
Hmm… Wasn’t the Six-Scripted Lantern Festival today?

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:21.600
Here?

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:25.080
Our hideout, or…

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:29.180
Secret hideout, or… Well, it’s our headquarters.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.330
I know.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.810
You sure are stupid, aren’t you?

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:35.500
Ojou just didn’t have a body.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.400
She was always close by, right?

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.090
Right, of course.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.500
What’s up, Hime?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.590
Shut up!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:47.560
Maybe because everyone’s paying attention to Ojou…

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:48.820
Are you sulking?

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.790
Hmph!

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.910
How is it, Ojou? Isn’t it the same?

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:56.980
It doesn’t feel right.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.060
It’s a little different.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.430
Where?

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:02.160
I have no idea.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.630
Little more to the right.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.310
The computer?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.280
There we go.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.530
I’m relieved!

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.640
You don’t have to be so startled.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.960
I won’t do anything.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:32.180
I’m called Kinya, Tsuzuki Kinya.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.540
Call me Kin-chan, just for fun.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.650
Can I help you?

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.820
I was just wondering whether you needed help or not.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.520
Waiting for the first train, right?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.140
It’s pretty dangerous around here.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.510
I’ll lend you taxi money.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.630
Really?

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:55.080
Where do you live?

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.030
Do you know where Saigawara is?

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:59.020
Saigawara?!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.150
I do, but…

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.270
Saigawara, eh? That’s really far…

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.440
Right?

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.300
Then wanna come to my store?

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.290
What?

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.260
Welcome…

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.800
Hey senpai, where were you?

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.320
Sweets Present Festival

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.320
Win a Vacation to France

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.320
Today’s special items

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.640
I’m taking care of this girl until the first train.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.680
I’m Kashiwagi Hidemi.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.650
Oh.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:55.520
Senpai you’re into that, aren’t you?

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.500
Eh?

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.200
Like that other girl you dragged in the other day.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.660
Are you a dumb-ass?

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:06.960
I mean, that time she was with you.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:12.190
I’ve decided to protect that girl all night long.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.270
What’s that?

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.360
When you’re nice to someone.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.200
You’re not at the bottom of existence.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.430
It means you still have things to spare.

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:23.990
You can believe that.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:27.000
That’s kind of cool.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.150
Right?

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.460
Um… should I pay?

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.350
It’s fine, since we were going to throw it out in two hours anyway.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:44.380
Even though you’re a delinquent, you
don’t look like you’d go out at night.

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.770
I’m no delinquent!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.810
I had a general test in cram school in the city today!

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:54.230
After some tea with old friends we started talking.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:58.570
And when I hurriedly rode the subway, it went the opposite way from Shinjuku.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.490
I realized and returned, but the train left.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:04.450
I dropped my cell phone and it broked. That’s why-

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.740
Don’t get so argumentative! It was a joke!

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.800
No one thinks you’re a delinquent.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:19.620
Wow! Are you really that smart?

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.180
No, not at all.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.970
Second in your grade level is amazing!

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:29.310
How lucky. I have no academic skills.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.660
I’m so pathetic you’d never forget me.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:36.260
After failing with the Sevens of the Multiplication Tables, I didn’t go to school much at all.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.080
Hah…

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.350
Hey, you laughed didn’t you?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:41.190
No, no I didn’t!

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:42.610
Really?

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.150
Yes, really.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:46.600
I’m speaking strangely!

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.630
To say the truth, just now

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.580
I was going to call home, but didn’t.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.790
Huh?

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:01.500
I couldn’t believe myself doing this.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.650
It’s a bit different from “fun”, but…

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.590
I don’t really understand,

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:11.690
but I think you shouldn’t be here.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.240
Or else, you’ll become like me.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.410
I understand.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:36.050
I’m really fine by myself.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.700
I said I’ll take you to the station.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:43.550
Isn’t that Kashiwagi?

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.810
Let’s get a picture of this defining moment!

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.020
Oh no!

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.080
It’s that girl.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:34.840
That girl! Kashiwagi Hidemi from 2-B!

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:37.470
It’s her, right?

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:39.870
What?

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.990
That girl’s being talked about on the secret forums.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.190
See? Look!

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.190
Second highest grades in her grade,

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.960
but doing something like this?

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.990
You can’t judge people by how they look.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:56.380
See you!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:57.320
Bye bye!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:58.950
Bye bye!

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.450
What’s she planning to do?

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:14.140
Yuzuki-san can now sense who’s planning to access the Hell Correspondence.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.470
I bet she’s trying to stop her.

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.380
That’s an impossible order.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.770
Hatred, Suffering, and Envy.

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:28.400
Like legs of a cauldron, they say they
become a support for people’s hearts.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.570
They don’t say that.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.340
She’ll probably realize eventually.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.490
The vanity of the road she chose.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:39.660
That might be Ojou’s goal.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:51.260
Kashiwagi Hidemi-san.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.690
Right?

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.290
Who are you?

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.390
Don’t ask me anything.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.540
Aren’t you trying to access the Hell Correspondence?

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:09.000
Because of that photo my life has become a mess.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:10.910
Mom and Dad…

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:14.150
Don’t believe me.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.580
The one who posted it on the secret forum was probably…

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.070
…someone in my own class.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.500
If I figure out their name, I’ll ask Jigoku Shoujo.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:26.670
Don’t! That’s the one thing you shouldn’t do!

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.510
Why? I-

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.270
My friend was ferried to Hell!

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:33.920
That girl…

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:37.260
…wasn’t bad at all! But-

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:48.070
Whatever reason you have you 
shouldn’t ferry people to Hell.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.180
There’s bound to be another way.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:55.730
Let’s look for it.

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:57.460
I’ll help!

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.720
Do you remember where that convenience store is?

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:01.530
Yes.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:05.660
But I wonder if Kinya-san will listen to my story.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:07.790
He was a nice person, right?

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:11.070
It’ll be fine, if he knew you were in trouble.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:14.510
He’ll probably tell everyone nothing happened.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.540
Of course.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.510
Why are you doing this?

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:28.430
I heard that you’ve got a ton of money.

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:30.860
What are you talking about?

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.610
I can see why you’re wearing a coat in the summer!

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:36.850
Be quiet and hand it over!

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.740
Stop! It was an exaggeration!

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:39.640
Shut up!

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:41.020
Hey there! What are you doing?!

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.500
{Aniki! Aniki!}Big brother! Big brother!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:52.970
Don’t be so pitiful! Haven’t I told you?

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:56.930
I’ll become a big-shot and strut around this Shinjuku!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.750
Getting caught by the police only increases my prestige.

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:01.510
Be quiet and get in!

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:03.190
While we’re at it,

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:07.000
I’m going to tell you everything I’ve done so far.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.020
I look forward to tomorrow’s enjoyment.

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:12.980
We’ve arrested Tsuzuki Kinya for assault.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:13.520
I repeat.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:14.910
Big brother,

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.130
Hey there!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.280
you’re so cool!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.190
What? Just some punk’s street fight?

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:24.410
It’s not him, right?

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:27.490
It can’t be!

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:30.180
What should I do?

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.000
If he went on the papers…

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.170
Wait!

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:53.180
Jigoku… Shoujo?

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:56.160
Ichimoku Ren.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.910
OK, Ojou.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:03.990
Take this.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:15.780
If you really want to enact revenge.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.840
Pull the red string.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:22.590
Pulling the string signifies a formal contract with me.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:27.550
The one you hate will swiftly go to Hell.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:33.540
But if you do, you have to pay the price.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:35.670
Curse someone, and two holes are created.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.530
If you agree to the contract

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:39.900
your soul too, will fall to Hell.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:41.030
To Hell?

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.840
Barred from Heaven,

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:49.470
your soul experiencing pain and suffering

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:51.790
will wander forever.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:59.800
The rest is up to you.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.910
Jigoku Shoujo!

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:11.060
Return her… return Akie!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:13.080
That’s impossible.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:14.300
Why?

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:17.070
See for yourself.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.370
The Last Days of Hatred.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:28.020
Hidemi-chan!

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:33.030
There he is!

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:35.040
Catch him! There he is!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.850
You! Come here!

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.290
I’ll kill you! Come here!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:40.880
Stop, Kinya-san!

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:43.380
What? Who are you?

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:45.640
Why do you know my name?

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:49.210
You’re wasting my time!

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.590
You don’t remember, do you?

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:53.140
I said, who are you?

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.140
You don’t remember.

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:00.430
Don’t, Hidemi-chan!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:02.250
What? Hidemi…

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.980
Hey, you’re from…!

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:06.950
It’s too late.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:13.980
Your grudge has been received.

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:25.940
Ai,

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:28.730
I’ll leave your Nagajuban here.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.940
Thanks, grandma.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:04.360
What?

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:05.300
What is this?

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.820
Oh, look.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.260
Are you OK?

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:21.800
Help me!

00:20:57.630 --> 00:20:58.640
Help me!

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.110
Stop kidding!

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:09.820
I didn’t believe I could be a big-shot!

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:12.700
I really…

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.150
O pitiful shadow, lost in darkness.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:19.610
Scarring people and degrading them.

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:22.390
The ball of karma is drowned in sin.

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:28.380
This once would you like to die?

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:36.150
It’s all a failure.

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:39.220
Even though I was so nice to her!

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:41.890
You’re so small!

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:42.630
You little…!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.550
Whimsical kindness used…

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:46.040
I don’t know!

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:46.040
…carelessly.

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:49.960
This hatred will ferry you to Hell.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.960
I always wanted to be a small-fry!

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.010
You must be tired!

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:59.690
Oh, Hidemi-chan!

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:16.750
<i>But I won’t give up.</i>

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:32.760
<i>This many people…?</i>

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:49.820
Your hatred shall be released.

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:49.820
Note: Candle says,  Kashiwagi Hidemi.

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:22.010
Your name?

00:24:22.010 --> 00:24:24.170
Shinohara Usagi.

00:24:24.170 --> 00:24:27.230
Everyone’s kind to you.

00:24:27.230 --> 00:24:27.980
That’s not true.

00:24:28.810 --> 00:24:31.690
They just can’t keep watching me,

00:24:31.690 --> 00:24:34.480
since I’m so dull.

00:24:35.030 --> 00:24:36.530
A tortoise.

00:24:37.770 --> 00:24:39.960
Even though I could do it, too.

00:24:40.780 --> 00:24:43.300
Even though I want to do things.

00:24:43.300 --> 00:24:45.200
But… because of that…

00:24:45.570 --> 00:24:48.400
Next Time: The Tortoise and the Hare.

00:24:50.610 --> 00:24:55.600
